---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="DNS Monitoring - Know the Moment Your Records Change"
  description="DNS monitoring, in development: scheduled checks of your records, change alerts with diffs, nameserver drift, and expiry warnings. Join early access."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Product</p>
      <span class="rounded-full border border-warn/40 bg-warn/10 px-3 py-0.5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-warn">In development - join early access</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
      Know the moment your DNS changes.
    </h1>

    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">DNS monitoring is the continuous re-checking of a domain’s records against their last known values, so a vendor-side change or unauthorized edit surfaces in hours instead of after the outage.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Records to monitor</h2>
    <section class="not-prose my-4" aria-label="Reference table">
      <div class="glass rounded-2xl p-5 shadow-lg sm:p-7 overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="pdns-table" style="width:100%">
          <thead><tr><th>Record</th><th>Drift meaning</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">A / AAAA</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Redirected or down</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">MX</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Mail broken</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">NS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Delegation moved</td></tr><tr><td class="font-medium text-ink">Mail auth</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Degraded</td></tr></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-ink-dim">
      Wrong MX after a migration. A CNAME deleted by a teammate. SPF quietly broken by a vendor
      change. DNS breaks silently and you find out from users. Monitoring watches your records on
      a schedule and tells you what changed, when, and what it affects.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <a href="/early-access/" class="btn-cta btn-shimmer px-5 py-2.5 text-sm">Join early access</a>
      <a href="/dns-propagation-checker/" class="border border-line bg-panel-2 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-ink hover:border-accent/40">Check propagation free, now</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2">
      {[
        {
          title: 'Record change alerts',
          desc: 'A, AAAA, MX, TXT, SPF, DKIM selectors, DMARC, CAA, NS - checked on a schedule. When a value changes, you get the diff, not just "something changed".',
        },
        {
          title: 'Email authentication drift',
          desc: 'The vendor you included in SPF changed their records and pushed you over the 10-lookup limit. Catch it before receivers do.',
        },
        {
          title: 'Nameserver and delegation drift',
          desc: 'Alerts if your domain\'s nameservers change, a dangling record appears, or DNSSEC validation breaks.',
        },
        {
          title: 'Expiry warnings',
          desc: 'SSL certificate and domain expiry checks with alerts at 30/14/7 days - so renewal never surprises you.',
        },
      ].map((f) => (
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 p-5">
          <h2 class="font-display font-semibold text-ink">{f.title}</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">{f.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="rich-text mt-14">
      <h2>Free today, before launch</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/dns-propagation-checker/" class="text-accent">DNS Propagation Checker</a> - see what resolvers worldwide serve right now.</li>
        <li><a href="/dns-record-lookup/" class="text-accent">DNS Record Lookup</a> - any record type, public resolvers.</li>
        <li><a href="/spf-record-checker/" class="text-accent">SPF Record Checker</a> - lookup count and validity, term by term.</li>
        <li><a href="/dnssec-checker/" class="text-accent">DNSSEC Checker</a> - validation chain status.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Early access</h2>
      <p>
        Monitoring is being built now, alongside
        <a href="/dmarc-monitoring/" class="text-accent">DMARC report monitoring</a>.
        Early-access members get the first accounts - <a href="/early-access/" class="text-accent">request access</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What does DNS monitoring check?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The records that break sites when they drift: A, AAAA, MX, NS, SPF, DKIM, DMARC, and DNSSEC, re-checked on a fixed schedule against their last known values.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How often are domains re-checked?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Every 6 hours in the current early-access build, with an email alert when any monitored record changes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens when a record changes?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">You get an alert with the old and new values, so a vendor-side change or an unauthorized edit surfaces in hours instead of after the outage.</p></details></div>
      </div>
</BaseLayout>
